.\" ai-tools-typesafe.conf(5) -- the TypeSafe credential file of the typesafe integration.
.\" @AI_TOOLS_VERSION@ is substituted at deploy time (install.sh install_subst
.\" and the RPM %prep), like ai-tools(1). The validation described here is the
.\" one the decide command applies when it reads the file.
.TH AI-TOOLS-TYPESAFE.CONF 5 "" "ai-tools @AI_TOOLS_VERSION@" "Agent Tools Restricted"
.SH NAME
ai-tools-typesafe.conf \- the credential and endpoint the typesafe integration sends a listing to
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/ai-tools/endpoints/typesafe.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
The typesafe integration lets a sandboxed session hand a long listing (a
grep, a git log, a checker's findings) to TypeSafe's bounded classifier
and get back the lines that bear on the task it states.
This file holds the API key that call is made with, and names the host it
may be sent to.
The decide command reads it at call time, and a session is handed the file's
path alone, so the key is in no session's environment.
.PP
The file is read only in a session launched with
.B typesafe
named in
.B AI_TOOLS_INTEGRATIONS
in
.BR ai-tools-operator.conf (5).
The shipped file has the key commented, so installing and enabling the
integration does not make a request until an operator sets it: the command reports
the file as not configured and does not print a result, and the session
falls back to the listing it already holds.
.PP
The file holds a credential, so it is owned by
.B root
in group
.B ai-tools
at mode
.BR 0640 :
root and the sandbox account read it, and no other account does.
Edit it with
.BR sudo .
The command refuses a file that is world-readable, world-writable, or a
symlink, and a key that still holds the template placeholder.
.PP
Only the documented options are read; any other key in the file is
ignored.
A value outside its documented form is refused with the configuration
status, and the command does not fall back to the default: a mistyped
threshold would otherwise change what is kept without a line saying so.
The file is parsed with the grammar
.BR ai-tools-operator.conf (5)
describes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI TYPESAFE_API_KEY= KEY
The API key TypeSafe issued, a single printable token.
Required: with it commented or empty the command exits with the
configuration status and does not print a result.
.TP
.BI TYPESAFE_MODEL= MODEL
The model that answers, a single token.
The shipped file names a versioned model rather than the moving alias
.BR jev-latest ,
because the alias changes answers on a release and the integration's
measurements are made against one version.
.TP
.BI TYPESAFE_BASE_URL= URL
The API origin: an
.B https://
URL with no path, query, or fragment.
Defaults to the vendor's public endpoint when unset.
.TP
.BI TYPESAFE_ENDPOINT_HOST= HOST
The host the key may be sent to.
Defaults to the vendor's public host.
The base URL's host must equal it, or the command refuses the call before
any request is made: a key is sent only to a host this file names twice, so
a base URL edited to another host does not carry the key there on its own.
.TP
.BI TYPESAFE_THRESHOLD= P
The least probability, from 0 to 1, that a listing line satisfies the task
for the line to be kept.
Defaults to 0.5.
.TP
.BI TYPESAFE_UNCERTAIN_BAND= LOW , HIGH
The inclusive band of probability reported as uncertain on the summary
line, as two probabilities with
.I LOW
no greater than
.IR HIGH .
Defaults to
.BR 0.35,0.65 .
.TP
.BI TYPESAFE_TIMEOUT_MS= MS
The time one request attempt may take, in whole milliseconds from 1000 to
120000.
Defaults to 15000.
The command bounds a whole call separately, so a retry does not extend it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ai-tools/endpoints/typesafe.conf
The shipped credential file, inert until the key is set.
An upgrade keeps the operator's copy.
.TP
.I /opt/ai-tools/integrations/typesafe/usage.log
One line per call made with
.BR \-\-usage\-log ,
which the shipped skill passes: counts, the model that answered, tokens,
elapsed time and the outcome.
No task text, no listing line, and no key is written there.
.SH EXAMPLES
The public endpoint with the shipped model:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=apikey_0123456789abcdef
TYPESAFE_MODEL=jev-1.13.0
.EE
.RE
.PP
Enable the integration, in
.BR ai-tools-operator.conf (5):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
AI_TOOLS_INTEGRATIONS=typesafe
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ai\-tools (1),
.BR ai-tools-operator.conf (5),
.BR ai\-tools\-providers (5)
